{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794538532490,"sessionID":"ses_e2d2be925ffe6LNNMoIS3b6D11","part":{"id":"prt_1d2d4ee8a001X5pQeTNLYGTSEC","sessionID":"ses_e2d2be925ffe6LNNMoIS3b6D11","messageID":"msg_1d2d4e8080013NnKV7oKOxahRN","type":"step-start","snapshot":"d6e0f3d117d8ad591b84cae1afb997d9b06a26a2"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794538532905,"sessionID":"ses_e2d2be925ffe6LNNMoIS3b6D11","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2d4ee8d001Rrw60UjuEaIH4D","sessionID":"ses_e2d2be925ffe6LNNMoIS3b6D11","messageID":"msg_1d2d4e8080013NnKV7oKOxahRN","type":"tool","id":"call_b6fd1671159b4129a1b373cd","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":110,"offset":270,"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md, lines 270-379\n270: ```\n271: \n272: ---\n273: \n274: ## 12. CHOOSING AN EMBEDDER\n275: \n276: The skill-advisor `semantic_shadow` lane runs against a pluggable embedder layer. As of phase `003/006` the contract surface (adapter interface, types, manifest registry, Ollama adapter) lives in `@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`, which the advisor now owns. Skill-advisor's local `runtime/lib/embedders/` files are thin re-export shims plus a skill-advisor-specific `schema.ts` integration that targets the package-local SQLite database at `runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite`. This section is the new-user onboarding view; the canonical embedder narrative lives at [embedder-pluggability.md](../system-spec-kit/references/memory/embedder-pluggability.md).\n277: \n278: ### 12.1 Current active default\n279: \n280: The persisted default is the `'auto'` sentinel. On daemon startup, `ensureActiveEmbedder()` invokes the shared cascade and persists the winner to `vec_metadata`. The cascade probes (in order):\n281: \n282: | Tier | Probe | Picks |\n283: | --- | --- | --- |\n284: | 1 | Ollama running with a known text manifest pulled | `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` (first match in priority list) |\n285: | 2 | hf-local model server reachable (pure-Node `@huggingface/transformers` HTTP client, zero Python) | `nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5` (hf-local) |\n286: | 3 | `OPENAI_API_KEY` present | `text-embedding-3-small` (1536-dim) |\n287: | 4 | `VOYAGE_API_KEY` present | `voyage-code-3` (1024-dim, acknowledged compromise for prose memory) |\n288: \n289: If every probe fails the daemon logs a warning and `semantic_shadow` scoring may degrade. The cascade only fires when the persisted pointer is `'auto'` or references a manifest the shared registry no longer knows about (legacy `embeddinggemma-300m` from a pre-phase-007 install). Manual `setActiveEmbedder()` calls take precedence — they pin the pointer and the cascade skips on subsequent restarts.\n290: \n291: Phase `002/jina-swap-and-reindex` runbook plus phase `004/skill-graph-db-writer-cross-wire` together make the swap safe end-to-end. The writer dispatcher (`refreshSkillEmbeddings()`) routes through `refreshSkillEmbeddingsViaAdapter` when an active pointer is set and falls back to the legacy `createEmbeddingsProvider` factory only when the cascade has not yet resolved (e.g. cold start before any probe succeeds).\n292: \n293: ### 12.2 Registered alternatives\n294: \n295: Source of truth: [`@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/registry.ts`](../system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/registry.ts). Skill-advisor's local `runtime/lib/embedders/registry.ts` is a re-export shim — adding manifests is a single edit in the shared package. The seven text-tuned manifests registered today, each as a frozen `EmbedderManifest`:\n296: \n297: | Name | Dim | Backend | Ollama tag | Max input | Notes |\n298: | --- | ---: | --- | --- | ---: | --- |\n299: | `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` | 768 | `ollama` | `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | 5000 | 768-dim retrieval specialist. Local-first cascade default per ADR-014. Uses `search_query: ` / `search_document: ` prefix tokens. |\n300: | `mxbai-embed-large-v1` | 1024 | `ollama` | `mxbai-embed-large:latest` | 1200 | Phase `016/004` paraphrase-strong candidate. |\n301: | `bge-small-en-v1.5` | 384 | `ollama` | `bge-small-en-v1.5:latest` | n/a | Compact 33M-param baseline. |\n302: | `bge-large-en-v1.5` | 1024 | `ollama` | `bge-large-en-v1.5:latest` | n/a | BAAI flagship retrieval model. |\n303: | `jina-embeddings-v3` | 1024 | `ollama` | `hf.co/gaianet/jina-embeddings-v3-GGUF:Q4_K_M` | 8000 | Multilingual + paraphrase-tuned. Matryoshka representation allows 256 / 512 / 768 / 1024 truncation. |\n304: | `bge-m3` | 1024 | `ollama` | `bge-m3:latest` | 8000 | Multilingual hybrid (dense + sparse + colbert). |\n305: | `snowflake-arctic-embed-l-v2.0` | 1024 | `ollama` | `snowflake-arctic-embed2:latest` | 8000 | Snowflake late-2024 flagship. 8192 context, multilingual, top MTEB retrieval scores. |\n306: \n307: > **Content-type split.** The TS shared registry is text-tuned by design. The `contentType: 'text' \\| 'code'` parameter on the shared cascade preserves the conceptual split for any future TS code consumer. The previous skill-advisor-specific `jina-embeddings-v2-base-code` entry was removed because it was code-tuned and did not belong in a text-only registry.\n308: \n309: Adding a new candidate is a single registry row in the shared package plus, if the backend is new, a single adapter under `shared/embeddings/adapters/`. No call sites change. The adapter contract (`EmbedderAdapter` in `@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/adapter.ts`) is small — `embed()` plus `ready()`.\n310: \n311: ### 12.3 Swap mechanism: `'auto'` sentinel + `setActiveEmbedder()`\n312: \n313: There are two operator-facing surfaces. **Neither is an environment variable.**\n314: \n315: **Sentinel-driven (default).** `vec_metadata` starts unpopulated; `getActiveEmbedder()` returns `{ name: 'auto', dim: 0 }`. The first daemon start invokes `ensureActiveEmbedder()` which calls the shared cascade and persists the winner. Subsequent daemon starts read the persisted pointer and skip the cascade.\n316: \n317: **Manual override.** [`setActiveEmbedder()`](./runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts) writes a specific manifest into `vec_metadata` and creates the matching `vec_<dim>` table:\n318: \n319: ```typescript\n320: import Database from 'better-sqlite3';\n321: import { setActiveEmbedder } from './runtime/dist/.../lib/embedders/schema.js';\n322: \n323: const db = new Database('.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite');\n324: setActiveEmbedder(db, 'jina-embeddings-v3', 1024);\n325: ```\n326: \n327: Effect of the call:\n328: \n329: - `vec_metadata.active_embedder_name` -> `jina-embeddings-v3`\n330: - `vec_metadata.active_embedder_dim` -> `1024`\n331: - `vec_1024` table created (if absent), schema `(skill_id, embedding BLOB, model_id, content_hash, updated_at)`\n332: - `hasActiveEmbedderPointer(db)` returns `true`, so both read path (`semantic-shadow.ts`, `loadSkillEmbeddings()`) and write path (`refreshSkillEmbeddingsViaAdapter`) target `vec_<active.dim>`\n333: - The shared cascade is skipped on subsequent restarts (a manual override pins the pointer)\n334: \n335: There are intentionally no embedder-administration commands here. Skill-advisor's surface is one database helper plus the cascade-driven sentinel. Operator discipline owns any manual swap workflow; there is no async re-index orchestrator on the skill-advisor side.\n336: \n337: ### 12.4 Operator-safe swap runbook\n338: \n339: The writer cross-wire shipped in phase `004` and the cascade-driven default shipped in phase `003/006`. The pointer flip is now safe end-to-end:\n340: \n341: 1. Stop the daemon.\n342: 2. Snapshot `runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite`.\n343: 3. (Optional) Call `setActiveEmbedder()` to override the cascade choice.\n344: 4. Restart the daemon. `ensureActiveEmbedder()` either honours your override or runs the cascade. The first scan or watcher tick populates `vec_<active.dim>` via the adapter dispatcher.\n345: 5. Smoke-test `advisor_recommend` through the CLI against three queries (`\"memory save\"`, `\"code search\"`, `\"spec folder\"`) and confirm top-3 picks are sane.\n346: \n347: The full runbook (snapshot + stop + override + restart + smoke test + rollback) is documented at [`002-jina-swap-and-reindex/evidence/swap-runbook.md`](../../<spec-folder>). The \"Architecture Context\" and \"Half-wired state\" sections are now historical — the half-wired state was closed by phase `004`.\n348: \n349: ### 12.5 Device selection\n350: \n351: Skill-advisor does not ship an explicit `_resolve_device()` shim. Device selection inherits from the underlying backend:\n352: \n353: | Backend | Device handling |\n354: | --- | --- |\n355: | `ollama` (default after cascade picks tier 1) | Ollama owns runtime device handling. It already covers Metal / CUDA / CPU autonomously based on its own daemon configuration. |\n356: | `hf-local` (fallback tier 2) | Pure-Node `@huggingface/transformers` HTTP model server (zero Python). Device handling (MPS / CUDA / CPU) is resolved by the model server's own runtime. |\n357: | `api` (OpenAI or Voyage fallback) | Remote inference; device handling is the provider's concern. |\n358: \n359: If you need MPS-style auto-detect for a local model, the Ollama backend already provides it on Apple Silicon by default — install Ollama, pull a manifest, the cascade picks it.\n360: \n361: ### 12.6 Cross-references\n362: \n363: - Canonical shared-embedder narrative: [`embedder-pluggability.md`](../system-spec-kit/references/memory/embedder-pluggability.md) — covers skill-advisor and the shared design rationale.\n364: - Shared contract surface: [`@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`](../system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/) — the canonical adapter, types, registry and Ollama adapter.\n365: - Shared cascade: [`@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts`](../system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts) — file-locked Ollama → hf-local → OpenAI → Voyage probe chain (ADR-014 local-first). Accepts optional `contentType: 'text' \\| 'code'` parameter (default `'text'`).\n366: - Skill-advisor schema helpers: [`runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts`](./runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts).\n367: - Architecture-gap follow-on: packet `003/006-shared-embedder-logic-with-spec-memory` (shipped phase 003/006).\n368: \n369: ---\n370: \n371: ## 13. RELATED RESOURCES\n372: \n373: | Document | Purpose |\n374: | --- | --- |\n375: | [README.md](./README.md) | Operator overview, quick start, runtime integrations. |\n376: | [ARCHITECTURE.md](./ARCHITECTURE.md) | Package-local architecture and public API entrypoints. |\n377: | [Hook reference](./hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md) | Prompt-time hook surfaces for each runtime. |\n378: | [Manual testing playbook](./manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md) | OP-001 / OP-002 operator scenarios + indexer edge cases. |\n379: | [Embedder pluggability narrative](../system-spec-kit/references/memory/embedder-pluggability.md) | Canonical embedder-pluggability reference. |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 380]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md, lines 270-379\n270: ```\n271: \n272: ---\n273: \n274: ## 12. CHOOSING AN EMBEDDER\n275: \n276: The skill-advisor `semantic_shadow` lane runs against a pluggable embedder layer. As of phase `003/006` the contract surface (adapter interface, types, manifest registry, Ollama adapter) lives in `@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`, which the advisor now owns. Skill-advisor's local `runtime/lib/embedders/` files are thin re-export shims plus a skill-advisor-specific `schema.ts` integration that targets the package-local SQLite database at `runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite`. This section is the new-user onboarding view; the canonical embedder narrative lives at [embedder-pluggability.md](../system-spec-kit/references/memory/embedder-pluggability.md).\n277: \n278: ### 12.1 Current active default\n279: \n280: The persisted default is the `'auto'` sentinel. On daemon startup, `ensureActiveEmbedder()` invokes the shared cascade and persists the winner to `vec_metadata`. The cascade probes (in order):\n281: \n282: | Tier | Probe | Picks |\n283: | --- | --- | --- |\n284: | 1 | Ollama running with a known text manifest pulled | `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` (first mat