{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794538569210,"sessionID":"ses_e2d2be925ffe6LNNMoIS3b6D11","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2d57c30001z2neJeyWyCEN6f","sessionID":"ses_e2d2be925ffe6LNNMoIS3b6D11","messageID":"msg_1d2d54956001h3cuWwA7PHqfkZ","type":"tool","id":"call_788ea2fbc76441bab20024ad","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"cost|Coin|plan\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt | head -40"},"output":"3:This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:skill-advisor <target>`: startup questions, the route manifest display, setup prompts, the rebuild plan and approval, diagnostic dashboards, result templates, troubleshooting, and next-step text. The command router owns target resolution and asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n87:| `embedder` | `doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` | mutates | Set up meaning matching for commands: probe Ollama and the model, show each step's cost and undo, and change nothing before a yes |\n119:Render the plan after the probe, before any write.\n132:With `--dry-run`, follow the plan with `Dry run: nothing was written.` and `STATUS=OK`.\n209:Render these blocks for `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`. The probe runs first and changes nothing. Every value is printed as the probe or the cost script returned it, and an unread value stays unread.\n213:Render after the read-only probe and before the plan.\n230:Render one row per missing step, in dependency order. A step the probe found present is not listed and is not run. Each cost comes from `measure-embedder-cost.mjs` or, when the cost script cannot run, from the install guide with a note that the live measurement was unavailable.\n238:| Install Ollama (printed only, never run by this route) | [the install guide's cost] | [the package manager's uninstall command] |\n239:| Start ollama serve in the background | [.memory.serveRssKb from the cost script] resident | Stop the pid this run started |\n240:| Pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5 | [.model.sizeBytes from the cost script] on disk | ollama rm nomic-embed-text:v1.5 |\n241:| Run skill_graph_scan to write the command vectors | [the scan's own runtime] plus [.warm.medianMs from the cost script] per embedded prompt | None, the database is derived state and a rerun rewrites it |\n251:Ask once, after the plan is on screen. Nothing is pulled, started or written before the answer, and approve is the only answer that proceeds.\n254:Set up meaning matching now? Only the steps in the plan run.\n256:   [one line per approved step with its cost]\n258:Never: an Ollama install or upgrade, a model the plan did not list, a model removal, a second server\n273:With `--dry-run`, stop after the plan, before the approval, and render this block.\n278:[the plan table, with each missing step's cost and undo]\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3:This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:skill-advisor <target>`: startup questions, the route manifest display, setup prompts, the rebuild plan and approval, diagnostic dashboards, result templates, troubleshooting, and next-step text. The command router owns target resolution and asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n87:| `embedder` | `doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` | mutates | Set up meaning matching for commands: probe Ollama and the model, show each step's cost and undo, and change nothing before a yes |\n119:Render the plan after the probe, before any write.\n132:With `--dry-run`, follow the plan with `Dry run: nothing was written.` and `STATUS=OK`.\n209:Render these blocks for `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`. The probe runs first and changes nothing. Every value is printed as the probe or the cost script returned it, and an unread value stays unread.\n213:Render after the read-only probe and before the plan.\n230:Render one row per missing step, in dependency order. A step the probe found present is not listed and is not run. Each cost comes from `measure-embedder-cost.mjs` or, when the cost script cannot run, from the install guide with a note that the live measurement was unavailable.\n238:| Install Ollama (printed only, never run by this route) | [the install guide's cost] | [the package manager's uninstall command] |\n239:| Start ollama serve in the background | [.memory.serveRssKb from the cost script] resident | Stop the pid this run started |\n240:| Pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5 | [.model.sizeBytes from the cost script] on disk | ollama rm nomic-embed-text:v1.5 |\n241:| Run skill_graph_scan to write the command vectors | [the scan's own runtime] plus [.warm.medianMs from the cost script] per embedded prompt | None, the database is derived state and a rerun rewrites it |\n251:Ask once, after the plan is on screen. Nothing is pulled, started or written before the answer, and approve is the only answer that proceeds.\n254:Set up meaning matching now? Only the steps in the plan run.\n256:   [one line per approved step with its cost]\n258:Never: an Ollama install or upgrade, a model the plan did not list, a model removal, a second server\n273:With `--dry-run`, stop after the plan, before the approval, and render this block.\n278:[the plan table, with each missing step's cost and undo]\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"cost|Coin|plan\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794538568752,"end":1794538569210}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794538571004,"sessionID":"ses_e2d2be925ffe6LNNMoIS3b6D11","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2d57938001U4jdH1i3br1hDW","sessionID":"ses_e2d2be925ffe6LNNMoIS3b6D11","messageID":"msg_1d2d54956001h3cuWwA7PHqfkZ","type":"tool","id":"call_5abfd797f0264b8f80c71be6","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"INSTALL-GUIDE.md.*12\\.|12\\.6|12\\.5\" --glob '!**/node_modules/**' -g '*.md' -g '*.ts' -g '*.cjs' -g '*.yaml' . | grep -i \"install-guide\\|section 12\" | head -20"},"output":"./specs/cli-classifier/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/002-advisor-jev-tiebreak-arm/scratch/w3-build/logs/39.pre.md:146:The `semantic_shadow` lane runs against the pluggable embedder layer in `@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`, which the advisor owns. The registry holds text-tuned embedding models and defaults through a local-first cascade to a local model when no embedder is explicitly set. For the full model registry, the cascade tier table and the swap workflow, see `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` §12.\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:174:The `semantic_shadow` lane runs against the pluggable embedder layer in `@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`, which the advisor owns. The registry holds text-tuned embedding models and defaults through a local-first cascade to a local model when no embedder is explicitly set. For the full model registry, the cascade tier table and the swap workflow, see `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` §12.\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:349:### 12.5 Device selection\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:361:### 12.6 Cross-references\n./specs/system-speckit/memory-search-and-knowledge/001-graph-and-context-optimization/changelog/003-memory-and-causal-runtime/changelog-003-006-shared-embedder-logic-with-spec-memory.md:49:- `INSTALL_GUIDE.md` section 12.6 cross-reference now matches section 12.1 and `auto-select.ts`: Ollama to hf-local to OpenAI to Voyage (ADR-014 local-first order)\n./specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/001-system-speckit-v4/035-v4-changelog-draft-update/scratch/changelog-digests/mcp-obsidian.md:33:A documentation-versus-reality drift fix. The `obsidian` MCP manual is live in `.utcp_config.json` and the `obsidian_OBSIDIAN_*` keys are in `.env.example`, but nine passages across six files still described that registration as pending a later gated phase, so the narration was moved to the present tense in `SKILL.md` §3 and §4, `README.md`, `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` §4, `references/troubleshooting.md`, `references/mcp-tools.md` and `mcp-servers/obsidian-mcp/README.md`. The agent prohibition against auto-modifying `.utcp_config.json`, `.env.example`, `opencode.json` and hub files was preserved verbatim in intent and only its stale justification clause changed. `README.md` frontmatter jumped 0.12.0.0 to 0.18.0.0 after drifting 5 releases behind `SKILL.md`. RENAME of a link target: the `README.md` §9 link `feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md` became `feature-catalog/FEATURE-CATALOG.md` to match the on-disk filename, since the lowercase form resolved on case-insensitive macOS but would 404 on a case-sensitive Linux or CI checkout. `SKILL.md` went 0.17.0.0 to 0.18.0.0.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/z_archive/010-skill-advisor-embedder-stack/003-install-guide-docs/implementation-summary.md:55:- §12.5 Device selection — honest note that skill-advisor does NOT ship an `_resolve_device()` shim; backend-inherited (Ollama handles Metal/CUDA/CPU on its own; llama-cpp baseline inherits from the shared provider cascade).\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/z_archive/010-skill-advisor-embedder-stack/003-install-guide-docs/implementation-summary.md:56:- §12.6 Cross-references — links to canonical narrative, mk-spec-memory analog, adapter contract, schema helpers, and the `010/004` follow-on.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/z_archive/010-skill-advisor-embedder-stack/003-install-guide-docs/implementation-summary.md:93:- **No false MPS auto-detect claim.** Skill-advisor inherits device handling from its backends (Ollama or the shared provider cascade) and does NOT ship its own `_resolve_device()` shim. The canonical narrative's MPS section is CocoIndex-specific. §12.5 documents this honestly to avoid implying an Apple Silicon optimization that does not exist on this side.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/z_archive/010-skill-advisor-embedder-stack/005-shared-embedder-logic-with-spec-memory/tasks.md:56:- [x] T010 [P0] Step 5: update skill-advisor `INSTALL_GUIDE.md` section 12 and `README.md`'s pluggable-layer subsection. Shipped in `5d1ed78ae1`; the section 12.6 cascade-ordering contradiction (P1-2) was fixed in the same-day remediation commit `23e7b6b6b3`.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"./specs/cli-classifier/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/002-advisor-jev-tiebreak-arm/scratch/w3-build/logs/39.pre.md:146:The `semantic_shadow` lane runs against the pluggable embedder layer in `@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`, which the advisor owns. The registry holds text-tuned embedding models and defaults through a local-first cascade to a local model when no embedder is explicitly set. For the full model registry, the cascade tier table and the swap workflow, see `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` §12.\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:174:The `semantic_shadow` lane runs against the pluggable embedder layer in `@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`, which the advisor owns. The registry holds text-tuned embedding models and defaults through a local-first cascade to a local model when no embedder is explicitly set. For the full model registry, the cascade tier table and the swap workflow, see `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` §12.\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:349:### 12.5 Device selection\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:361:### 12.6 Cross-references\n./specs/system-speckit/memory-search-and-knowledge/001-graph-and-context-optimization/changelog/003-memory-and-causal-runtime/changelog-003-006-shared-embedder-logic-with-spec-memory.md:49:- `INSTALL_GUIDE.md` section 12.6 cross-reference now matches section 12.1 and `auto-select.ts`: Ollama to hf-local to OpenAI to Voyage (ADR-014 local-first order)\n./specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/001-system-speckit-v4/035-v4-changelog-draft-update/scratch/changelog-digests/mcp-obsidian.md:33:A documentation-versus-reality drift fix. The `obsidian` MCP manual is live in `.utcp_config.json` and the `obsidian_OBSIDIAN_*` keys are in `.env.example`, but nine passages across six files still described that registration as pending a later gated phase, so the narration was moved to the present tense in `SKILL.md` §3 and §4, `README.md`, `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` §4, `references/troubleshooting.md`, `references/mcp-tools.md` and `mcp-servers/obsidian-mcp/README.md`. The agent prohibition against auto-modifying `.utcp_config.json`, `.env.example`, `opencode.json` and hub files was preserved verbatim in intent and only its stale justification clause changed. `README.md` frontmatter jumped 0.12.0.0 to 0.18.0.0 after drifting 5 releases behind `SKILL.md`. RENAME of a link target: the `README.md` §9 link `feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md` became `feature-catalog/FEATURE-CATALOG.md` to match the on-disk filename, since the lowercase form resolved on case-insensitive macOS but would 404 on a case-sensitive Linux or CI checkout. `SKILL.md` went 0.17.0.0 to 0.18.0.0.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/z_archive/010-skill-advisor-embedder-stack/003-install-guide-docs/implementation-summary.md:55:- §12.5 Device selection — honest note that skill-advisor does NOT ship an `_resolve_device()` shim; backend-inherited (Ollama handles Metal/CUDA/CPU on its own; llama-cpp baseline inherits from the shared provider cascade).\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/z_archive/010-skill-advisor-embedder-stack/003-install-guide-docs/implementation-summary.md:56:- §12.6 Cross-references — links to canonical narrative, mk-spec-memory analog, adapter contract, schema helpers, and the `010/004` follow-on.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/z_archive/010-skill-advisor-embedder-stack/003-install-guide-docs/implementation-summary.md:93:- **No false MPS auto-detect claim.** Skill-advisor inherits device handling from its backends (Ollama or the shared provider cascade) and does NOT ship its own `_resolve_device()` shim. The canonical narrative's MPS section is CocoIndex-specific. §12.5 documents this honestly to avoid implying an Apple Silicon optimization that does not exist on this side.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/z_archive/010-skill-advisor-embedder-stack/005-shared-embedder-logic-with-spec-memory/tasks.md:56:- [x] T010 [P0] Step 5: update skill-advisor `INSTALL_GUIDE.md` section 12 and `README.md`'s pluggable-layer subsection. Shipped in `5d1ed78ae1`; the section 12.6 cascade-ordering contradiction (P1-2) was fixed in the same-day remediation commit `23e7b6b6b3`.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"INSTALL-GUIDE.md.*12\\\\.|12\\\\.6|12\\\\.5\\\" --glob '!**/node_modules/**' -g '*.md' -g '*.ts' -g '*.cjs' -g '*.yaml' . | grep -i \\\"install-guide\\\\|section 12\\\" | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794538567992,"end":1794538571004}}}}
