{"type":"text","timestamp":1794538628612,"sessionID":"ses_e2d2be925ffe6LNNMoIS3b6D11","part":{"id":"prt_1d2d64a6b0010R99v7rgMEAtNb","sessionID":"ses_e2d2be925ffe6LNNMoIS3b6D11","messageID":"msg_1d2d63d3b001rhTwZ7ZFvkYxCc","type":"text","text":"## Files written\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md` (18 insertions, 0 deletions)\n  - Section 2 (PREREQUISITES), line 54: one bullet stating `/doctor:install` sets up the embedder by default, its checklist runs `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`, which prints the cost and asks before pulling the model or starting the server, and a no leaves a phrase-only install.\n  - New subsection `### 12.7 Setup route and cost`, lines 370-385: the setup route (probes `command -v ollama`, `/api/version`, `/api/tags`, `advisor_status --include-semantic-health true`, plan with cost and undo per step, one approval, `STATUS=CANCELLED` on a no, `STATUS=OK` after the plan under `--dry-run`, Ollama install printed and never run), the cost table taken from the phase scratch runs (disk 274302450 bytes / 261.6 MiB, idle serve RSS 25776 KB / 25.2 MiB, loaded runner RSS 279520 KB / 273.0 MiB, 5 minute Ollama keep-alive unload, warm 4.8 ms median / 8.9 ms p95, cold first call 538.53 ms, measured 2026-11-13), and the fact that `skill_graph_scan` writes the `vec_cmd_<dim>` vectors while `skill-graph.sqlite` is derived state ignored by `.gitignore` (`runtime/database/*.sqlite`).\n\n## Verify output\n\n```\n$ rg -n \"skill-advisor embedder|vec_cmd\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md\n54:- `/doctor:install` sets up the embedder by default: its checklist includes `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`, which prints the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server, so answering no leaves a phrase-only install.\n372:`/doctor:install` includes the embedder setup by default, and the setup itself runs as `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` from inside the target repo. The route probes `command -v ollama`, `/api/version`, `/api/tags` and `advisor_status --include-semantic-health true`, prints one plan row per missing step with its cost and its undo, and asks once before it runs anything. A no stops with `STATUS=CANCELLED` and changes nothing. `--dry-run` prints the plan and stops with `STATUS=OK`. The route never installs or upgrades Ollama: it prints the install command for the operator, and the install guide owns that cost.\n385:Once the approved steps ran, the route runs `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json`. That scan is what writes the command vectors into the `vec_cmd_<dim>` table: without it `commandVectorCoverage.embedded` stays at zero and the semantic lane reports off. The database is derived state and gitignored, since `.gitignore` ignores `runtime/database/*.sqlite`, so the scan costs its own runtime plus the warm latency per embedded prompt and leaves nothing for git.\nexit=0\n```\n\n3 lines printed, requirement was at least two.\n\nCross-checked every table number against the scratch runs with a script: `274302450`, `4.8`, `8.9` (from `cost-warm.json`), `25776`, `538.53` (from `cost-cold.json`) and `279520` (loaded runner RSS in `cost-warm.json`) all appear in the guide. `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short` for the file shows only `M` on `INSTALL-GUIDE.md`, and the diff is additions only, so nothing else was touched. The tasks.md checkbox was left unticked.\n\n## Not done / notes\n\n- `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` had no meaning-matching cost table yet, so the table here uses the same dimensions T034 names (disk, idle memory, loaded memory, 5 minute unload, warm and cold latency) over the same two scratch files, which is what \"the same cost table\" resolves to.\n- Nothing else was blocked.","time":{"start":1794538621547,"end":1794538628612}}}
